cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this package, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "spectralDEMATEL: Spectral Diagnostics for DEMATEL Influence Matrices"
abstract: >-
  Computes the spectral diagnostics of a DEMATEL influence matrix: coupling and
  the total-effect multiplier, indirect and mode dominance, three readings of
  hierarchy, the entry and accumulation profiles, the eigenvalue condition
  number, a permutation surrogate baseline, and the closed-form derivative of
  the dominant eigenvalue in every off-diagonal entry. The package computes and
  returns data. It does not draw, read files, or print, so it can be driven
  equally from a script, a batch job, or a browser-side application compiled to
  WebAssembly.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Delias
    given-names: Pavlos
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3722-2307"
    affiliation: "Democritus University of Thrace"
# The concept DOI, matching the README badge and inst/CITATION. Deliberately not
# a version DOI: this file is read by whoever arrives at the repository, and the
# newest release is what they should cite unless they need to pin a number.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21849277
repository-code: "https://github.com/pdelias/spectralDEMATEL"
url: "https://pdelias.r-universe.dev/spectralDEMATEL"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - DEMATEL
  - multi-criteria decision analysis
  - spectral analysis
  - eigenvalue sensitivity
  - influence matrix
  - R
  - WebAssembly
